-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  std_hookio_stream_setvbuf.adam - setvbuf / setbuf from C on a virtual
  file and on a real file of the same bytes (PaskalCPP's std_hookio
  TestStreamSetvbuf)

  10000 bytes, every variant (std_hookio_c_svset: unbuffered, sizes with
  and without the caller's array, bad mode and size, setbuf, mid-read,
  after an ungetc) through "rt", "r" and "rb": every slot equals the real
  file's, the caller's array included (what the CRT filled it with shows
  each fill's size); variant 23 (setvbuf inside the backup area) keeps the
  stream where the caller stands (glibc has no real twin: it reads freed
  memory). Then fflush on a reading handle (ucrt's nothing) against a real
  file, and stdout's flush before a line-buffered fill.
*******************************************************************************/

